// The player's mother, after the first morning.
=== start
[flag epo_out] -> home
[flag hostages_left] -> left
[quest hostages=reported] -> after
[quest hostages=summoned] -> summoned
"You're still here." It isn't quite a complaint.
-> hub

=== summoned
"Vellaunos is waiting. The hall, {name}. Not tomorrow."
-> hub

=== hub
* "Tell me about Eponina." -> epona
* [!flag mother_gift] "I'll need things for the road." -> gift
* [quest hostages active] "I'm going to find her." -> going
* "Later." -> END

=== epona
She was nine when they took her. She'll be fourteen now. "She bit the Roman who lifted her onto the cart. Did you know that? Bit him through the glove. He laughed. He said she'd do well."

Your mother looks at the door. "I don't know what that means, 'do well.' I've had five years to think about it."
* "I'll find out." -> hub
* "Mother." -> hub

=== gift
~ set mother_gift; give herbs 2; give bread 2; silver 10
She has it ready already, wrapped in a cloth: bread, a twist of dried herbs, ten silver coins that you know were for the spring sowing.
"Don't argue. Don't you dare."
* Take it. -> hub

=== going
"Don't tell me. Do it." She turns back to the fire. "And come back. Both of you. I mean both."
* Go. -> END

=== after
"Noviodunum." She tries the name and doesn't like it. "Is that far?"
* "Far enough." -> after2
* "Not so far." -> after2

=== after2
She nods slowly. "Then go. Bring her back, and don't you dare send word you're dead. Come and tell me yourself."
* Go. -> END

=== home
[flag mother_home_seen] -> home2
~ set mother_home_seen; xp 50
Your mother is sitting at the hearth with Eponina's head in her lap, combing her short Roman hair with her fingers, over and over, as if she could make it grow. She doesn't get up. She looks at you over your sister's head, and her face does something it hasn't done in five years.

"You came and told me yourself," she says. "Good. Good."

Eponina, without opening her eyes: "I bit him again, Mother. Nearly. I wanted to."
* Sit down with them. -> home2

=== home2
"Sit," your mother says. "Eat. You're thin." She hasn't let go of Eponina's hair. "She talks in her sleep in Latin. I don't care. Let her talk."
* "I will." -> END

=== left
"You saw her." Your mother's hands are still. "She's alive. She can read, you said. In two languages." She turns back to the fire. "Then she's worth something to them. They'll keep her. You'll go back."

It isn't a question.
* "I'll go back." -> END
